l","content":[{"type":"text","text":""}]}]}]}]},"e":"Modal class = the class with the highest frequency: 40 ≤ s < 50 (18 students). Median class: n = 50, so the median lies between the 25th and 26th values. Cumulative frequency up to 40 ≤ s < 50 is 18, and up to 50 ≤ s < 60 it is 28, so both the 25th and 26th students sit in 50 ≤ s < 60.\\n\\nAnswer: C","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Grouped Frequency Tables","cfg":{"source":"myp4-full-formal-assessment-2026","question_number":21,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"A","next_time_hint":"Highest frequency for the mode; cumulative frequency for the median.","assessment_style":"formal_assessment","option_labels":["The modal class contains 18 students and the median class is at position 25","Modal class 40 ≤ s < 50; median class 40 ≤ s < 50","Modal class 40 ≤ s < 50; median class 50 ≤ s < 60","Modal class 40 ≤ s < 50; median class 60 ≤ s < 70"],"option_key":[3],"hints":["Which class has the biggest f?","The median of 50 students lies at position 25 — find which class the 25th value falls in."]},"marking":""},{"n":22,"t":"single_choice","p":"The lengths, in centimetres, of 30 fish caught by a fishing cooperative in Ada are grouped as shown. Estimate the median length, to 1 decimal place.","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The lengths, in centimetres, of 30 fish caught by a fishing cooperative in Ada are grouped as shown. Estimate the median length, to 1 decimal place."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Length L, in centimetres"}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Frequency f"}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cumulative frequency"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"10 ≤ L < 20"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"4"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"20 ≤ L < 30"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"9"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"13"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"30 ≤ L < 40"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"11"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"24"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"40 ≤ L < 50"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"30"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total frequency"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"30"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":""}]}]}]}]},"e":"n = 30, so the median is the 15.5th value — inside the 30 ≤ L < 40 class (cf up to the previous class is 13). Estimated median = 30 + (15.5 − 13) ÷ 11 × 10 = 30 + 2.27 ≈ 31.8 cm. (Using n ÷ 2 = 15 gives 30 + (15 − 13) ÷ 11 × 10 ≈ 31.8 cm as well.)\\n\\nAnswer: D","m":1,"df":"medium","tp":"Grouped Frequency Tables","cfg":{"source":"myp4-full-formal-assessment-2026","question_number":22,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"A","next_time_hint":"Find the median class from cumulative frequency, then interpolate.","assessment_style":"formal_assessment","option_labels":["30.0 cm","35.0 cm","40.0 cm","31.8 cm"],"option_key":[4],"hints":["The median position is n ÷ 2 = 15 — which class contains the 15th value?","Median = L + (n÷2 − previous CF) ÷ f × width."]},"marking":""},{"n":23,"t":"single_choice","p":"Daily sales of a provision shop, in cedis, over 50 days are grouped in the table. A student estimated the mean sales by calculating (20 + 40 + 60 + 80) ÷ 4 = 50. Which error explains her working?","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Daily sales of a provision shop, in cedis, over 50 days are grouped in the table. A student estimated the mean sales by calculating (20 + 40 + 60 + 80) ÷ 4 = 50. Which error explains her working?"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Daily sales d, in cedis"}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Frequency f"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"20 ≤ d < 40"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"8"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"40 ≤ d < 60"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"14"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"60 ≤ d < 80"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"16"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"80 ≤ d < 100"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"12"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total frequency"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"50"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":""}]}]}]}]},"e":"The numbers 20, 40, 60, 80 are the lower class boundaries of the four classes — not the midpoints (30, 50, 70, 90) — and averaging them gives every class the same weight. Her estimate 50 ignores both the midpoints and the frequencies.\\n\\nAnswer: C","m":1,"df":"medium","tp":"Grouped Frequency Tables","cfg":{"source":"myp4-full-formal-assessment-2026","question_number":23,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"C","next_time_hint":"Compare 20, 40, 60, 80 with the midpoints.","assessment_style":"formal_assessment","option_labels":["She used the class widths instead of the class midpoints.","She used the upper class boundaries and then divided by the total frequency.","She used the lower class boundaries as the values and gave every class the same weight, ignoring the frequencies.","She used the class midpoints correctly but divided by the number of classes instead of by the total frequency."],"option_key":[3],"hints":["What are the midpoints of 20 ≤ d < 40, 40 ≤ d < 60, …?","Check whether she used the frequencies at all."]},"marking":""},{"n":24,"t":"single_choice","p":"The travel time to school, in minutes, of 60 students in a class is grouped as shown. Estimate the mean travel time, correct to 1 decimal place.","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The travel time to school, in minutes, of 60 students in a class is grouped as shown. Estimate the mean travel time, correct to 1 decimal place."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Travel time t, in minutes"}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Frequency f"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"0 ≤ t < 10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"6"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"10 ≤ t < 20"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"18"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"20 ≤ t < 30"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"21"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"30 ≤ t < 40"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"10"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"40 ≤ t < 50"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"5"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total frequency"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"60"}]}]}]}]},"e":"Midpoints: 5, 15, 25, 35, 45. Σfx = 