urve to find how many students scored less than 30 marks."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/exam-figures/myp4/q26_ogive.jpg","alt":"Ogive of the marks of 60 students","width":96}}]},"e":"On the curve, the point above mark 30 sits at cumulative frequency 25. So 25 students scored less than 30 marks.\\n\\nAnswer: B","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Cumulative Frequency Curves","cfg":{"source":"myp4-full-formal-assessment-2026","question_number":26,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"A","next_time_hint":"Read the y-value directly above 30 on the mark axis.","assessment_style":"formal_assessment","option_labels":["15 students","25 students","45 students","20 students"],"option_key":[2],"hints":["Go up from 30 on the horizontal axis to the curve.","The height you land on is the cumulative frequency — read it off the vertical axis."],"figure":"myp4_q26_ogive"},"marking":""},{"n":27,"t":"single_choice","p":"A student copies this table of the shopping times of 50 customers in a supermarket in Accra and has to complete the cumulative frequency column. Which value belongs in the empty cell?","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A student copies this table of the shopping times of 50 customers in a supermarket in Accra and has to complete the cumulative frequency column. Which value belongs in the empty cell?"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Time t (minutes)"}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Frequency f"}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cumulative frequency"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"0 ≤ t < 10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"6"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"text","text":"10 ≤ t < 20"}]},{"type":"tableCell","cont